# CODEOWNERS — starter. Scaffolded by RavenClaude's /init-agent-ready (gold-standard
# GitHub protocol tier). Everything here is COMMENTED OUT: uncomment a line, replace
# the placeholder owner with a real @user / @org/team, and commit.
#
# Path-scoped ownership: each line is "<path-pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]". The
# LAST matching pattern wins for a given file, so put the broadest rule first and
# narrower overrides below it. An owner must have write access or the rule is ignored.
# Place this file at the repo root, in .github/, or in docs/.
#
# Enforcement is separate: listing an owner here only REQUESTS their review. To make
# a code-owner's approval REQUIRED to merge, turn on code-owner review in the branch
# ruleset — the companion setup-branch-protection.sh --require-codeowner-review sets
# require_code_owner_review:true.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-permissions-and-settings/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# ── Examples (uncomment + edit) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Default owners for everything in the repo (broadest — keep it first):
# *                       @OWNER-PLACEHOLDER
#
# Scope a directory to a team:
# /src/                   @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/backend
# /docs/                  @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/docs
#
# Guard the CI + dependency surface with extra reviewers (narrower — put below *):
# /.github/               @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/platform
# /.github/workflows/     @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/platform @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/security
# package.json            @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/platform
# go.mod                  @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/platform
# go.sum                  @ORG-PLACEHOLDER/platform
